% A bound query over a rule holding an aggregate: the rewrite adorns the
% rule and reads the group, and everything its body reads, completely.  A
% query that folds a group and calls a rewritten predicate with the result
% bound copies the aggregate into the seed of the call's magic rule, which
% reads the query's group relation: the group is filled before any
% generated rule runs.  A body of one atom is folded over the atom's own
% relation, which is read completely too, even where the query also calls
% the atom's predicate bound; and two rules alike but for the column their
% fold is keyed on are two rules, which the rewrite does not merge.
edge(a, b). edge(a, c). edge(b, c). edge(c, a). edge(c, b). edge(c, d).
node(a). node(b). node(c). node(d).

outdeg(X, N) :- node(X), N = count { edge(X, Y) }.
path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- path(X, Y), edge(Y, Z).
reach(X, N) :- node(X), N = count { path(X, Y) }.
degree(X, N) :- node(X), N = count { edge(X, Y) }.
degree(X, N) :- node(X), N = count { edge(Y, X) }.

outdeg(a, N)?
reach(d, N)?
N = count { edge(X, _) }, outdeg(Y, N)?
N = count { node(X) }, reach(Y, N)?
path(a, Y), N = count { path(Y, Z) }?
degree(c, N)?
